# Known bug: a way a permanent grants to cast from the graveyard (CR 601.3, 118.9) is judged on the whole Room card, mana value 8
# there (CR 709.4b), and never on a door, so Serra Paragon's "permanent spell with mana value 3 or less" cannot cast Unholy Annex from the graveyard.
# CR 709.3 and its rulings: casting a Room is choosing a door to cast, only that door's characteristics are considered ("you could cast
# Bottomless Pool this way, but not Locker Room"), and that door is the one unlocked as it enters (CR 709.5d). Unholy Annex ({2}{B}, mana value
# 3) is castable; Ritual Chamber ({3}{B}{B}) is not. The engine offers neither and has no way to name the door of a granted cast.
# Bot1 casts Unholy Annex on turn 1, Serra Paragon the same turn, on turn 3 Disenchants its own Room, and on turn 5 casts Unholy Annex from the
# graveyard with the Paragon's permission; it enters with Annex's door unlocked, exiled if it dies (the Paragon's gift).

